            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to feel sorry, then the Marathi for to sob quietly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दिलासा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिलासा — dilāsā — \"comfort; reassurance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मित्राच्या फोनने मला खूप दिलासा मिळाला. mitrācyā phonne malā khūp dilāsā miḷālā. My friend's phone call was a great comfort to me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिलासा (dilāsā) देणे, to reassure; दिलासा (dilāsā) मिळणे, to be reassured, with the dative."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दिलासा (dilāsā) is a loan from Persian dilāsā, \"consolation\", built on dil, \"heart\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
